# What the Lambda functions need next to the runtime (Python 3.14, Linux x86_64), vendored into the
# deployment package by infra/lib/bundling.ts. lambda-requirements.txt is the pinned set with hashes
# the zip is built from (`uv pip install -r lambda-requirements.txt --require-hashes`); regenerate it
# with
#   uv pip compile lambda-requirements.in --python-version 3.14 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux2014 \
#     --only-binary :all: --generate-hashes -o lambda-requirements.txt
# and keep boto3/botocore on the version of agentcore/requirements.in and agentcore-lake/requirements.in.
#
# rdflib and pyparsing for the OWL explorer; boto3 with its dependencies because the boto3 of the
# Lambda runtime varies by Region and over time, and tab 3 needs a botocore with the `s3vectors`
# client (tab 2 the `bedrock-agentcore` one). No token library: IAM decides who may call the API's
# function URL (infra/lib/auth.ts).
rdflib==7.6.0
pyparsing==3.3.3
boto3==1.43.111
botocore==1.43.111
s3transfer==0.19.2
jmespath==1.1.0
